    pains: 'UK families face their own set of pressures: independent school fees crossing £20,000–£40,000 per year following the January 2025 VAT change, state-school place shortages in many catchments, the new Children\'s Wellbeing and Schools Bill changing the home education landscape from 2026, and a growing number of families wanting curriculum continuity through international moves. Smartious gives UK families and British diaspora families a serious alternative — a globally recognised online school with full Cambridge, Edexcel, IB and AQA exam pathways, live classes on UK time, and fees that come in under a quarter of comparable independent schools.',
    curricula: ['Cambridge IGCSE', 'Cambridge A-Level', 'IB Diploma', 'IB MYP', 'Pearson Edexcel International', 'AQA GCSE', 'British National Curriculum (Primary)'],
    regulation: 'Home education is legal across the entire United Kingdom. In England, Wales and Northern Ireland, parents have the right to educate their child at home under Section 7 of the Education Act 1996; deregistration from a state school is immediate upon written notice to the headteacher, and no Local Authority permission is required to begin. Scotland is different: where a child is enrolled at a local authority school, parental consent for withdrawal must be obtained from the council before home education begins. Across all four nations, parents must provide a "suitable, efficient, full-time education" — and Local Authorities may make informal enquiries to satisfy themselves this is happening. The Children\'s Wellbeing and Schools Bill 2026 introduces mandatory "Children Not in School" (CNIS) registers in England, requiring parents to provide basic details of their educational provision; this is a data-registration requirement, not an inspection regime. Smartious provides written provision reports, attendance records, predicted grades and termly progress documentation that satisfy LA enquiries and the new CNIS requirements.',
    examCentres: 'Cambridge IGCSE, Cambridge A-Level, Pearson Edexcel and AQA GCSE examinations are sat at private-candidate centres across the UK. Major centres include CIE Tutors London, Tutors and Exams (Manchester, Birmingham, Leeds, Sheffield, Bristol, Edinburgh, Glasgow), the British Council, and a growing number of independent schools that accept external candidates. Smartious handles all examination registration, advises on the right centre for each student, runs full mock examination programmes before the May/June and October/November series, and provides past papers, marking schemes and predicted-grade documentation that UCAS and exam boards require.',
    testimonial: '',
